Asked once, or asked everywhere
Two columns. On the left, the questions about a record's discipline answered by
whoever happens to write each path into the store: the import job, the
correction screen, the nightly clean-up, and the one written in a hurry. On the
right, the same questions declared once on the type itself: whether a version
may be replaced or only added to, whether every touch is audited, how long it
is kept at least and at most, and what identifies one.
